row(10, 13, 'MATERIAL', f'TO KEEP THE COMMANDMENTS OF THE LORD AND HIS STATUTES WHICH I COMMAND YOU TODAY, FOR YOUR GOOD. {HP(10, 13, (("לשמר", "את", "מצות", "יהוה", "ואת", "חקתיו"), "to keep the commandments of the LORD and His statutes — ONE seat of the pair in this form (\'the commandments of the LORD\' eight in the book)"), (("אשר", "אנכי", "מצוך", "היום"), "which I command you today — the singular formula\'s eighteen seats in the book (the plural six); 4:40 shares seven tokens"), (("לטוב", "לך"), "for your good — ONE seat of the form (6:24 \'for our good\'; the adjective with the prefix six in the Bible)"))} {AP(10, 13, (("למטר", "ית", "פקודיא", "דיי", "וית", "קימוהי"), "to keep the commandments of the LORD and His statutes"), (("לדייטב", "לך"), "that it be well with you"))} The fifth infinitive of the demand; \'I\' Moses\' (the store\'s \'?\' at the pronoun).')
